# UI Development Standards

This guide outlines the standards and best practices for UI development in the Weiqi.com project to ensure consistency across the application.

## Component Library

The project uses [shadcn/ui](mdc:https:/ui.shadcn.com) components built on top of Tailwind CSS and Radix UI. These components are located in [components/ui/](mdc:goweb/src/components/ui).

### Core UI Components

- [Button](mdc:goweb/src/components/ui/button.tsx) - Primary interactive element
- [Card](mdc:goweb/src/components/ui/card.tsx) - Container for related content
- [Dialog](mdc:goweb/src/components/ui/dialog.tsx) - Modal dialogs
- [Form](mdc:goweb/src/components/ui/form.tsx) - Form elements with validation
- [Input](mdc:goweb/src/components/ui/input.tsx) - Text input fields

## Styling Guidelines

### Theme System

The application uses a theme system with CSS variables defined in [globals.css](mdc:goweb/src/app/globals.css). The theme is managed through the [ThemeProvider](mdc:goweb/src/components/theme-provider.tsx).

```tsx
// Example of proper theme usage
import { ThemeProvider } from "@/components/theme-provider";

export function MyComponent({ children }) {
  return (
    <ThemeProvider attribute="class" defaultTheme="dark" enableSystem>
      {children}
    </ThemeProvider>
  );
}
```

### Color Palette

Always use the semantic color variables from the theme system:

- Background: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-sidebar`
- Text: `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`
- Accent: `bg-primary`, `bg-secondary`, `bg-accent`
- Status: `bg-destructive`

Avoid using hardcoded colors. Instead, use the CSS variables defined in the theme.

### Spacing and Layout

Follow these spacing guidelines:

- Use Tailwind's spacing scale (`p-4`, `m-2`, etc.)
- For component spacing, use consistent values:
  - Small spacing: `space-y-1`, `space-x-2`
  - Medium spacing: `space-y-4`, `space-x-4`
  - Large spacing: `space-y-8`, `space-x-6`

### Typography

- Headings: Use the appropriate heading level semantically
- Body text: Use `text-sm` or `text-base` with appropriate line height
- Use font weights consistently:
  - Regular text: `font-normal`
  - Emphasis: `font-medium`
  - Strong emphasis: `font-semibold`
  - Headings: `font-bold`

## Component Patterns

### Component Structure

Follow this structure for new components:

```tsx
// MyComponent.tsx
"use client"; // If using client-side features

import * as React from "react";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// Define props interface
interface MyComponentProps {
  // Props definition
}

export function MyComponent({ 
  className, 
  children,
  ...props 
}: MyComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div 
      className={cn("base-styles-here", className)}
      {...props}
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Variants Pattern

For components with multiple variants, use the class-variance-authority (cva) pattern:

```tsx
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority";

const myComponentVariants = cva(
  "base-styles-here",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "bg-primary text-primary-foreground",
        secondary: "bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground",
      },
      size: {
        default: "h-10 px-4",
        sm: "h-8 px-2",
        lg: "h-12 px-6",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "default",
      size: "default",
    },
  }
);

export interface MyComponentProps 
  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>,
    VariantProps<typeof myComponentVariants> {}
```

## Layout Patterns

### Page Structure

Follow this structure for page layouts:

```tsx
export default function PageName() {
  return (
    <div className="container py-8">
      <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Page Title</h1>
      <div className="grid gap-6">
        {/* Page content */}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Responsive Design

- Use the Tailwind responsive prefixes consistently:
  - Mobile-first approach (default)
  - Small screens: `sm:`
  - Medium screens: `md:`
  - Large screens: `lg:`
  - Extra large: `xl:`

Example:
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {/* Content */}
</div>
```

## Best Practices

1. **Component Composition**: Prefer composition over complex props
2. **Accessibility**: Ensure all components are accessible
   - Use semantic HTML elements
   - Include proper ARIA attributes
   - Ensure keyboard navigation works
3. **State Management**: Keep state as local as possible
4. **Performance**: 
   - Use React.memo for expensive components
   - Avoid unnecessary re-renders
5. **Naming Conventions**:
   - Components: PascalCase (e.g., `ButtonGroup`)
   - Hooks: camelCase with 'use' prefix (e.g., `useFormState`)
   - Utilities: camelCase (e.g., `formatDate`)

## Common Patterns

### Form Implementation

```tsx
import { zodResolver } from "@hookform/resolvers/zod";
import { useForm } from "react-hook-form";
import * as z from "zod";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Form, FormControl, FormField, FormItem, FormLabel, FormMessage } from "@/components/ui/form";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";

// Define schema
const formSchema = z.object({
  username: z.string().min(2).max(50),
});

export function ProfileForm() {
  const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof formSchema>>({
    resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),
    defaultValues: {
      username: "",
    },
  });

  function onSubmit(values: z.infer<typeof formSchema>) {
    // Handle form submission
  }

  return (
    <Form {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="space-y-8">
        <FormField
          control={form.control}
          name="username"
          render={({ field }) => (
            <FormItem>
              <FormLabel>Username</FormLabel>
              <FormControl>
                <Input placeholder="Username" {...field} />
              </FormControl>
              <FormMessage />
            </FormItem>
          )}
        />
        <Button type="submit">Submit</Button>
      </form>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

### Data Fetching

```tsx
"use client";

import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import { Skeleton } from "@/components/ui/skeleton";

export function DataComponent() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    async function fetchData() {
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/data');
        const result = await response.json();
        setData(result);
      } catch (error) {
        console.error("Error fetching data:", error);
      } finally {
        setLoading(false);
      }
    }
    
    fetchData();
  }, []);

  if (loading) {
    return <LoadingSkeleton />;
  }

  return (
    <div>
      {/* Render data */}
    </div>
  );
}

function LoadingSkeleton() {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-2">
      <Skeleton className="h-8 w-full" />
      <Skeleton className="h-8 w-full" />
      <Skeleton className="h-8 w-full" />
    </div>
  );
}
```

